# Line-based barrels: one self-contained entry per line, in no meaningful order, so two
# branches adding entries both keep theirs. Union merging keeps every line and never reports
# a clash, so it suits only files of that shape: no multi-line entries, and no lines that
# depend on each other.
#
# This works where git merges locally (merge, rebase). GitHub's own merge ignores it: its
# merge API answered 409 for exactly this case (measured 2026-11-02). When GitHub reports a
# conflict in one of these files, rebase onto main locally and push.
**/features/index.ts merge=union
